WEBVTT

00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:01.469
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:04.531 --> 00:00:06.511
Take your brother outside
as fast as you  can!

00:00:06.653 --> 00:00:07.633
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:10.750
Mary! No!

00:00:12.852 --> 00:00:13.873
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:15.241 --> 00:00:16.486
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:18.582 --> 00:00:20.010
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:21.806
I can't do this alone.

00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:25.086
No!

00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:29.025
We got work to do.

00:00:29.692 --> 00:00:32.121
This is dad's single
most valuable possession

00:00:32.162 --> 00:00:34.325
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:34.488 --> 00:00:36.407
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:36.529 --> 00:00:38.856
You know, saving people, hunting things,

00:00:38.931 --> 00:00:39.870
Family business.

00:00:39.911 --> 00:00:41.768
No. I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:41.788 --> 00:00:43.319
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.136
Sam, You know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:46.966 --> 00:00:47.946
Yeah. I know.

00:00:57.485 --> 00:00:59.403
Okay, your turn. Truth or dare?

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:00.479
Truth.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.152
Do you want to make
out with benji swartz?

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:05.091
Dare.

00:01:05.642 --> 00:01:06.806
Okay, lame.

00:01:07.718 --> 00:01:08.901
You have to...

00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:11.759
Say "bloody mary" in the bathroom.

00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:14.345
Is that the best you can come up with?

00:01:14.712 --> 00:01:15.855
Who's bloody mary?

00:01:16.365 --> 00:01:17.692
She's this witch.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.958
I heard she was a lady
killed in a car crash.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.815
It doesn't matter who she is.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.961
If you say her name three
times in the bathroom mirror,

00:01:25.777 --> 00:01:26.899
She appears...

00:01:27.593 --> 00:01:28.900
And scratches your eyes out!

00:01:31.656 --> 00:01:33.432
So why would anyone say it?

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:35.616
Because it isn't real.

00:01:37.044 --> 00:01:38.371
No turning on the lights.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:39.949
And remember,

00:01:40.112 --> 00:01:40.949
Three times.

00:02:06.765 --> 00:02:07.704
Bloody mary.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.785
This is so stupid.

00:02:14.791 --> 00:02:15.729
Bloody mary.

00:02:26.423 --> 00:02:27.444
Bloody mary.

00:02:38.146 --> 00:02:38.799
Scared you.

00:02:38.922 --> 00:02:40.105
You guys are jerks.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.065
Lily?

00:02:41.738 --> 00:02:42.779
You mind keeping it down?

00:02:43.657 --> 00:02:44.657
Sorry, daddy.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.494
Sorry, mr. Shoemaker.

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:26.191
You so like him!

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:28.899
Hey, geek.

00:03:29.144 --> 00:03:30.491
You guys having fun?

00:03:30.818 --> 00:03:32.103
You're out past curfew.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.669
Thanks, dad.

00:04:15.611 --> 00:04:16.754
Why Sam?

00:04:18.741 --> 00:04:19.353
No!

00:04:22.735 --> 00:04:24.551
Why Sam? Sam, wake up.

00:04:33.363 --> 00:04:35.261
I take it I was having a nightmare?

00:04:36.098 --> 00:04:37.649
Yeah, another one.

00:04:41.276 --> 00:04:42.746
Hey, at least I got some sleep.

00:04:42.909 --> 00:04:45.175
Hey, you know, sooner or later,
we're gonna talk about this.

00:04:46.134 --> 00:04:46.848
Are we here?

00:04:47.256 --> 00:04:49.726
Yep. Welcome to Toledo, Ohio.

00:04:53.421 --> 00:04:55.523
So, what do you think
really happened to this guy?

00:04:55.557 --> 00:04:57.170
So what we're gonna find out.

00:04:59.721 --> 00:05:00.517
Let's go.

00:05:29.742 --> 00:05:30.253
Hey.

00:05:30.987 --> 00:05:31.600
Hey.

00:05:33.008 --> 00:05:33.763
Can I help you?

00:05:34.416 --> 00:05:36.478
Yeah, we're the... med students.

00:05:36.985 --> 00:05:37.557
Sorry?

00:05:37.924 --> 00:05:38.822
Oh, doctor...

00:05:39.455 --> 00:05:41.067
Fliglavitch didn't tell you?

00:05:41.128 --> 00:05:43.026
We talked to him on the phone.

00:05:43.169 --> 00:05:44.394
We're from Ohio state.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.737
He's supposed to show
us the shoemaker corpse.

00:05:46.758 --> 00:05:47.513
It's for our paper.

00:05:47.778 --> 00:05:49.574
Well, I'm sorry, he's at lunch.

00:05:49.738 --> 00:05:50.391
Oh.

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:51.615
Well, he said, uh

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.064
Oh, well, you know, it doesn't matter.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:55.533
You don't mind showing
us the body, do you?

00:05:55.574 --> 00:05:56.798
Sorry, I can't.

00:05:57.002 --> 00:05:59.268
Doc will be back in an
hour. You can wait for him,

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:00.023
If you want.

00:06:00.186 --> 00:06:00.941
An hour?

00:06:02.312 --> 00:06:04.046
We got to be heading back to columbus.

00:06:04.108 --> 00:06:04.740
Yeah.

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:07.087
Look man, this paper's half our grade,

00:06:07.128 --> 00:06:08.904
So if you don't mind
helping us out? Look, man

00:06:10.159 --> 00:06:10.914
No.

00:06:13.302 --> 00:06:15.160
I'm gonna hit him in his face, I swear.

00:06:29.052 --> 00:06:30.093
Follow me.

00:06:33.985 --> 00:06:35.522
Dude, I earned that money.

00:06:35.639 --> 00:06:37.169
You won it in a poker game.

00:06:37.394 --> 00:06:38.190
Yeah.

00:06:38.904 --> 00:06:40.802
The newspaper said
his daughter found him.

00:06:41.204 --> 00:06:42.755
She said his eyes were bleeding.

00:06:42.837 --> 00:06:43.898
More than that.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:45.572
They practically liquefied.

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:52.385
Any sign of a struggle,
maybe somebody did it to him?

00:06:52.566 --> 00:06:53.239
Nope.

00:06:53.648 --> 00:06:55.342
Besides the daughter, he was all alone.

00:06:56.168 --> 00:06:57.805
What's the official causeof death?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.963
Doc's not sure. He's
thinking massive stroke,

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:02.554
Maybe an aneurysm.

00:07:03.232 --> 00:07:04.870
Something burst up in
there, that's for sure.

00:07:05.448 --> 00:07:06.337
What do you mean?

00:07:06.828 --> 00:07:08.606
Intense cerebral bleeding.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:11.389
This guy had more blooding his
skull than anyone I've ever seen.

00:07:12.325 --> 00:07:13.284
But the eyes?

00:07:13.635 --> 00:07:15.085
What would cause something like that?

00:07:15.283 --> 00:07:16.850
Capillaries can burst.

00:07:16.897 --> 00:07:18.862
See a lot of bloodshot
eyes with stroke victims.

00:07:19.213 --> 00:07:21.341
Yeah, you ever see exploding eyeballs?

00:07:21.879 --> 00:07:23.260
That's a first for me.

00:07:23.377 --> 00:07:25.037
But, hey, I'm not the doctor.

00:07:26.538 --> 00:07:28.644
Think we could take a
look atthat police report?

00:07:28.761 --> 00:07:30.398
You know, for our paper?

00:07:31.264 --> 00:07:33.603
I'm not really supposed to show you

00:07:37.702 --> 00:07:39.199
Might not be one of ours.

00:07:39.293 --> 00:07:41.257
Might just be some freak medical thing.

00:07:41.749 --> 00:07:43.198
How many times in dad's long

00:07:43.199 --> 00:07:46.333
And varied career has it actually
been a freak medical thing

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.554
And not some sign of an
awful supernatural death?

00:07:49.694 --> 00:07:51.636
Uh, almost never.

00:07:51.823 --> 00:07:52.829
Exactly.

00:07:52.946 --> 00:07:53.811
All right.

00:07:54.115 --> 00:07:55.628
Let's go talk to the daughter.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.414
Feel like we're underdressed.

00:08:24.761 --> 00:08:26.087
You must be Donna,right?

00:08:26.274 --> 00:08:26.883
Yeah.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.859
Hi, uh... We're really sorry.

00:08:31.748 --> 00:08:32.520
Thank you.

00:08:33.035 --> 00:08:34.976
I'm sam.This is dean.

00:08:35.871 --> 00:08:37.134
We worked with your dad.

00:08:38.467 --> 00:08:39.262
You did?

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:40.830
Yeah.This whole thing

00:08:41.625 --> 00:08:42.795
I mean, a stroke.

00:08:44.381 --> 00:08:46.322
I don't think she really wants
to talk about this right now.

00:08:46.323 --> 00:08:47.609
It's okay, I'm okay.

00:08:49.294 --> 00:08:50.674
Were there ever any symptoms?

00:08:50.791 --> 00:08:52.078
Dizziness, migraines?

00:08:53.154 --> 00:08:54.019
No.

00:08:55.233 --> 00:08:57.175
That's because it wasn't a stroke.

00:08:57.409 --> 00:08:58.415
Lily, don't say that.

00:08:58.672 --> 00:08:59.374
What?

00:09:00.169 --> 00:09:01.666
I'm sorry, she's just upset.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.654
No, it happened because of me.

00:09:03.725 --> 00:09:04.988
Sweetie, it didn't.

00:09:05.069 --> 00:09:05.865
Lily,

00:09:06.866 --> 00:09:08.621
Why would you saysomething like that?

00:09:09.559 --> 00:09:11.173
Right before he died,I said it.

00:09:11.875 --> 00:09:12.694
You said what?

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:15.922
Bloody Mary, three times
in the bathroom mirror.

00:09:19.353 --> 00:09:21.014
She took his eyes, that's what she does.

00:09:21.084 --> 00:09:23.494
That's not why dad
died.This isn't your fault.

00:09:24.219 --> 00:09:25.739
I think your sister's right,lily.

00:09:26.621 --> 00:09:28.749
There's no way it could
have been Bloody Mary.

00:09:29.896 --> 00:09:32.118
Your dad didn't say it,did he?

00:09:33.849 --> 00:09:35.322
No, I don't think so.

00:10:00.615 --> 00:10:01.972
Sam:The Bloody Mary legend

00:10:03.808 --> 00:10:06.299
Dad ever find any evidence
that it was a real thing?

00:10:07.094 --> 00:10:08.357
Not that I know of.

00:10:13.602 --> 00:10:14.397
I mean,

00:10:14.912 --> 00:10:15.988
Everywhere else,

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:21.126
All over the country,
kids will play Bloody Mary.

00:10:21.127 --> 00:10:23.373
And as far as we know,
nobody dies from it.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:25.209
Hey well, maybe everywhere
it's just a story,

00:10:25.232 --> 00:10:26.846
But here it's actually happening.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.530
The place where the legend began?

00:10:29.856 --> 00:10:32.079
But according to the legend,
the person who says...

00:10:35.166 --> 00:10:37.880
The person who says
you know what gets it

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:38.488
But here...

00:10:38.511 --> 00:10:40.055
Shoemaker gets it instead,yeah.

00:10:40.102 --> 00:10:40.710
Right.

00:10:41.739 --> 00:10:43.540
Never heard anything like that before.

00:10:44.352 --> 00:10:46.832
Still, the guy did die
right in front of the mirror.

00:10:47.031 --> 00:10:49.229
And the daughter's right.
The way the legend goes,

00:10:49.924 --> 00:10:51.772
"You know who" scratches your eyes out.

00:10:51.936 --> 00:10:53.292
It's worth checking into.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.479
What are you doingup here?

00:11:02.819 --> 00:11:03.590
We...

00:11:04.175 --> 00:11:05.555
We had to go to the bathroom.

00:11:06.585 --> 00:11:07.520
Who are you?

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:11.076
Like we said downstairs,
we worked with Donna's dad.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:13.953
He was a day trader or
something, he worked by himself.

00:11:14.236 --> 00:11:15.733
No, I know, I meant...

00:11:15.896 --> 00:11:17.955
And those weird questions downstairs,

00:11:18.914 --> 00:11:19.990
What was that?

00:11:22.072 --> 00:11:23.896
So you tell me what's going on

00:11:24.508 --> 00:11:25.654
Or I start screaming.

00:11:25.888 --> 00:11:27.011
All right, all right.

00:11:29.329 --> 00:11:31.411
We think something
happened to Donna's dad.

00:11:31.528 --> 00:11:32.604
Yeah, a stroke.

00:11:32.931 --> 00:11:34.756
That's not the sign of a typical stroke.

00:11:37.142 --> 00:11:38.639
We think it might be something else.

00:11:39.364 --> 00:11:40.129
Like what?

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:41.743
Honestly,

00:11:42.936 --> 00:11:43.965
We don't know yet.

00:11:45.088 --> 00:11:47.193
But we don't want it to
happen to anyone else.

00:11:47.661 --> 00:11:48.496
That's the truth.

00:11:49.408 --> 00:11:50.063
So,

00:11:50.601 --> 00:11:51.794
If you're gonna scream,

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:53.736
Go right ahead.

00:11:56.332 --> 00:11:57.331
Who are you, cops?

00:11:59.857 --> 00:12:00.746
Something like that.

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:01.869
I'll tell you what.

00:12:02.126 --> 00:12:02.781
Here.

00:12:03.249 --> 00:12:04.477
If you think of anything,

00:12:04.547 --> 00:12:06.489
You or your friends
notice anything strange,

00:12:06.769 --> 00:12:09.062
Out of the ordinary,
just give us a call.

00:12:17.529 --> 00:12:19.627
All right, say Bloody Mary
really is haunting this town.

00:12:19.651 --> 00:12:21.639
There's gonna be some sort of proof

00:12:21.733 --> 00:12:23.136
A local woman who died nasty.

00:12:23.276 --> 00:12:25.171
Yeah, but a legend this
wide spread, it's hard.

00:12:25.194 --> 00:12:27.532
I mean, there's like 50
versions of who she actually is.

00:12:27.533 --> 00:12:28.690
One story says she's a witch,

00:12:28.691 --> 00:12:30.866
Another says she's a mutilated bride.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:31.989
There's a lot more.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:33.720
What are we supposed to be looking for?

00:12:33.854 --> 00:12:35.679
Every version's got thingsin common.

00:12:35.702 --> 00:12:36.918
It's always a woman named Mary,

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:39.035
And she always dies
in front of a mirror.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.251
So we've got to search local newspapers

00:12:41.274 --> 00:12:43.192
Public records as far back as they go,

00:12:43.286 --> 00:12:45.157
See if we can find a
Mary who fits the bill.

00:12:45.789 --> 00:12:46.888
Well, that sounds annoying.

00:12:47.075 --> 00:12:48.689
No, it won't be so bad,

00:12:48.759 --> 00:12:49.718
As long as we...

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:52.556
I take it back.

00:12:53.234 --> 00:12:54.661
This will be very annoying.

00:12:57.702 --> 00:13:00.848
I'm not sure. They were cops
or detectives or something.

00:13:01.129 --> 00:13:03.047
Whoever they were, they were cute.

00:13:03.164 --> 00:13:03.912
Jill.

00:13:04.029 --> 00:13:04.989
You didn't think so?

00:13:05.224 --> 00:13:07.025
Yeah, okay,they were cute. But,

00:13:07.836 --> 00:13:10.760
Still,do you think something
could have happenedto Donna's dad?

00:13:10.894 --> 00:13:12.280
Maybe Lily was right.

00:13:12.882 --> 00:13:14.730
Maybe Bloody Mary got him.

00:13:15.666 --> 00:13:16.665
Very funny.

00:13:17.811 --> 00:13:19.729
Wait, I'm sorry.

00:13:20.454 --> 00:13:22.653
Was that fear I hear in your voice?

00:13:23.261 --> 00:13:24.033
No.

00:13:25.359 --> 00:13:26.178
Charlie...

00:13:26.412 --> 00:13:28.260
I'm walking to the
bathroom mirror right now.

00:13:29.149 --> 00:13:30.295
Jill, quit it.

00:13:33.003 --> 00:13:34.032
Oh, no,

00:13:34.383 --> 00:13:35.670
I can't help myself.

00:13:36.535 --> 00:13:37.822
I'm gonna say it.

00:13:38.898 --> 00:13:39.857
Bloody Mary.

00:13:40.692 --> 00:13:42.072
Bloody Mary.

00:13:43.055 --> 00:13:44.973
Bloody Mary.

00:13:47.352 --> 00:13:48.171
Jill?

00:13:53.107 --> 00:13:53.878
Jill!

00:13:58.422 --> 00:14:00.574
You're such a freak.
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:14:56.175 --> 00:14:57.321
You did it.

00:15:02.257 --> 00:15:03.695
You killed that boy.

00:15:23.741 --> 00:15:24.654
Why Sam?

00:15:29.581 --> 00:15:30.985
Why'd you let me fall asleep?

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.207
'Cause I'm an awesome brother.

00:15:35.317 --> 00:15:36.790
So, what did you dream about?

00:15:37.562 --> 00:15:39.387
Lollipops and candy canes.

00:15:41.094 --> 00:15:42.170
Yeah, sure.

00:15:46.605 --> 00:15:47.774
You find anything?

00:15:48.078 --> 00:15:50.464
Oh, besides a whole new
level of frustration?

00:15:50.979 --> 00:15:53.061
No. I've looked at everything.

00:15:55.158 --> 00:15:57.615
A few local women, a
Laura and a Catherine,

00:15:57.638 --> 00:15:59.463
Committed suicide in front of a mirror,

00:15:59.884 --> 00:16:01.935
And a giant mirror fell
on a guy named dave.

00:16:02.029 --> 00:16:02.918
But, uh...

00:16:04.064 --> 00:16:04.836
No Mary.

00:16:09.163 --> 00:16:10.824
Maybe we just haven't found it yet.

00:16:12.087 --> 00:16:14.192
I've also been searching
for strange deaths,

00:16:14.276 --> 00:16:15.843
In the area, you know,

00:16:16.197 --> 00:16:17.858
Eyeball bleeding, that sort of thing.

00:16:17.998 --> 00:16:19.027
There's nothing.

00:16:19.869 --> 00:16:21.834
Whatever's happening here,
maybe it just ain't Mary.

00:16:28.337 --> 00:16:29.039
Hello?

00:16:36.511 --> 00:16:39.295
And they found her
on the bathroom floor.

00:16:40.441 --> 00:16:43.435
And her-Her eyes...

00:16:44.956 --> 00:16:46.430
They were gone.

00:16:47.295 --> 00:16:48.161
I'm sorry.

00:16:50.453 --> 00:16:51.576
And she said it.

00:16:53.447 --> 00:16:54.937
I heard her say it.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.152
But it couldn't be because of that.

00:17:01.534 --> 00:17:02.633
I'm insane, right?

00:17:04.545 --> 00:17:05.644
No, you're not insane.

00:17:06.673 --> 00:17:09.457
God, that makes me feel so much worse.

00:17:10.432 --> 00:17:11.227
Look...

00:17:14.549 --> 00:17:16.245
We think something's happening here,

00:17:17.485 --> 00:17:19.075
Something that can't be explained.

00:17:20.191 --> 00:17:21.244
And we're gonna stop it,

00:17:22.437 --> 00:17:23.513
But we could use your help.

00:17:42.081 --> 00:17:43.578
What did you tell Jill's mom?

00:17:43.625 --> 00:17:46.245
I just said I needed some time alone
with Jill's pictures and things.

00:17:46.278 --> 00:17:46.980
Great.

00:17:47.471 --> 00:17:48.734
I hate lying to her.

00:17:49.389 --> 00:17:50.746
This is for the greater good.

00:17:50.793 --> 00:17:51.775
Hit the lights.

00:17:56.072 --> 00:17:57.499
What are you guys looking for?

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.784
We'll let you know
as soon as we find it.

00:17:59.854 --> 00:18:01.164
Hey, night vision.

00:18:03.036 --> 00:18:04.696
Thanks. Perfect.

00:18:07.974 --> 00:18:09.284
Do I look like Paris Hilton?

00:18:20.969 --> 00:18:22.700
So, I don't get it.

00:18:22.724 --> 00:18:25.133
I mean, the first victim
didn't summon Mary,

00:18:25.157 --> 00:18:26.794
And the second victim did.

00:18:27.145 --> 00:18:28.431
How's she choosing them?

00:18:28.969 --> 00:18:29.695
Beats me.

00:18:34.257 --> 00:18:36.245
I want to know why Jill
said it in the first place.

00:18:37.415 --> 00:18:38.444
It's just a joke.

00:18:38.811 --> 00:18:41.688
Somebody's gonna say it again.
It's just a matter of time.

00:18:54.372 --> 00:18:55.051
Hey.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:57.897
There's a black light
in the trunk, right?

00:19:20.591 --> 00:19:22.299
Gary Bryman?

00:19:23.936 --> 00:19:25.163
You know who that is?

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:27.222
No.

00:19:35.021 --> 00:19:38.202
So, Gary Bryman was an 8 year-Old boy.

00:19:39.115 --> 00:19:41.197
Two years ago, he was
killed in a hit and run.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:44.121
The car was described
as a black toyota camry,

00:19:44.722 --> 00:19:47.178
But nobody got the
plates or saw the driver.

00:19:47.506 --> 00:19:48.348
Oh, my god.

00:19:49.307 --> 00:19:49.915
What?

00:19:50.359 --> 00:19:51.763
Jill drove that car.

00:19:54.975 --> 00:19:56.729
We need to get back to
your friend Donna's house.

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:07.311
Linda shoemaker.

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.177
Why are you asking me this?

00:20:12.539 --> 00:20:14.567
Look, we're sorry, but it's important.

00:20:15.666 --> 00:20:16.321
Yeah.

00:20:16.622 --> 00:20:17.956
Linda's my mom, okay?

00:20:18.283 --> 00:20:20.178
And she overdosed on sleeping pills.

00:20:20.295 --> 00:20:21.979
It was an accident, and that's it.

00:20:25.311 --> 00:20:26.270
I think you should leave.

00:20:26.293 --> 00:20:28.071
Donna, just listen Get out of my house!

00:20:32.392 --> 00:20:33.304
Oh, my god.

00:20:34.591 --> 00:20:37.222
Do you really think her dad
could have killed her mom?

00:20:38.603 --> 00:20:39.538
Maybe.

00:20:40.151 --> 00:20:41.531
I think I should stick around.

00:20:43.168 --> 00:20:44.805
All right. Whatever you do, don't...

00:20:44.993 --> 00:20:47.308
Believe me, I won't say it.

00:20:51.618 --> 00:20:52.811
Wait, wait, wait.

00:20:53.116 --> 00:20:55.057
You're doing a nationwide search?

00:20:55.197 --> 00:20:55.829
Yep.

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:58.675
The NCIC, the FBI database

00:20:58.868 --> 00:21:02.084
Any mary in the country who died in
front of a mirror is good enough for me.

00:21:02.494 --> 00:21:05.464
But if she's haunting the town,
she should have died in the town.

00:21:05.623 --> 00:21:08.547
I'm telling you. There's nothing local. I
check. So, unless you've gota better idea.

00:21:08.659 --> 00:21:11.003
Why Mary's choosing a victim?
It seems like there's a pattern.

00:21:11.043 --> 00:21:12.245
I know I was thinking the same thing.

00:21:12.325 --> 00:21:14.329
With mr. Shoemaker
and Jill's hit and run

00:21:14.349 --> 00:21:15.871
Both had secrets where people died.

00:21:15.931 --> 00:21:16.432
Right.

00:21:16.512 --> 00:21:17.896
There's a lot of folklore about mirrors

00:21:17.897 --> 00:21:19.900
That they reveal or your
lies, or your secrets,

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:22.023
That they're a true
reflection of your soul,

00:21:22.024 --> 00:21:23.466
Which is why it's bad
luck to break them.

00:21:23.546 --> 00:21:24.408
Right. Right.

00:21:25.282 --> 00:21:26.644
Yeah, so maybe if you've got a secret,

00:21:26.664 --> 00:21:28.498
I mean, like a really nasty
one where someone died,

00:21:28.499 --> 00:21:30.903
Then mary sees it and
punishes you for it.

00:21:31.035 --> 00:21:32.736
Whether you summoned her or not.

00:21:33.619 --> 00:21:34.601
Take a look at this.

00:21:47.305 --> 00:21:48.908
Looks like the same handprint.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.073
Her name was Mary Worthington

00:21:51.896 --> 00:21:54.120
An unsolved murder in
Fort Wayne, Indiana.

00:21:56.346 --> 00:21:59.131
I was on the job for 35 years,

00:21:59.371 --> 00:22:00.653
Detective for most of that.

00:22:01.414 --> 00:22:03.778
Now, everybody packs it
in with a few loose ends,

00:22:03.861 --> 00:22:05.784
But the Mary Worthington murder...

00:22:07.647 --> 00:22:09.030
That one still gets me.

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:10.432
What exactly happened?

00:22:11.896 --> 00:22:13.619
You boys said you were reporters.

00:22:13.980 --> 00:22:15.542
We know Mary was 19,

00:22:15.685 --> 00:22:16.787
Lived by herself.

00:22:16.927 --> 00:22:18.730
We know she won a few beauty contests,

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:20.252
Dreamt of getting out of Indiana,

00:22:20.773 --> 00:22:21.715
Being an actress.

00:22:22.214 --> 00:22:24.258
And we know, the night of march 29th,

00:22:24.779 --> 00:22:26.161
Someone broke into her apartment

00:22:26.301 --> 00:22:27.143
And murdered her,

00:22:28.064 --> 00:22:29.266
Cut out her eyeswith a knife.

00:22:31.111 --> 00:22:31.872
That's right.

00:22:33.996 --> 00:22:36.240
See, sir, when we ask you what
happened, we want to know what

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:37.401
You think happened.

00:22:40.971 --> 00:22:43.956
Technically, I'm not supposed
to have a copy of this.

00:22:50.106 --> 00:22:50.707
Now,

00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:53.371
See that there,

00:22:53.952 --> 00:22:54.794

"T-R-E"?

00:22:55.295 --> 00:22:55.916
Yeah.

00:22:56.647 --> 00:22:59.333
I think Mary was trying to
spell out the name of her killer.

00:22:59.414 --> 00:23:00.395
You know who it was?

00:23:00.816 --> 00:23:01.838
Not for sure.

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:04.722
But there was a local man,

00:23:04.803 --> 00:23:05.684
A surgeon,

00:23:06.247 --> 00:23:07.269
Trevor Sampson.

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:09.833
And I think he cut her up good.

00:23:10.314 --> 00:23:12.372
Now, why would he do
something like that?

00:23:12.913 --> 00:23:15.096
Her diary mentioned
a man she was seeing.

00:23:15.860 --> 00:23:17.723
She called him by his initial, "T."

00:23:18.524 --> 00:23:19.226
Well,

00:23:19.887 --> 00:23:21.590
Her last entry,

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:24.915
She was gonna tell to his
wife about their affair.

00:23:25.137 --> 00:23:27.240
But how do you know it
was Sampson who killed her?

00:23:27.862 --> 00:23:29.164
It's hard to say.

00:23:31.750 --> 00:23:34.735
But the way her eyes were cut
out, it was almost professional.

00:23:35.897 --> 00:23:37.321
But you could never prove it?

00:23:37.442 --> 00:23:37.962
No.

00:23:38.443 --> 00:23:39.265
No prints,

00:23:39.365 --> 00:23:40.547
No witnesses.

00:23:41.388 --> 00:23:42.570
He was meticulous.

00:23:44.333 --> 00:23:45.395
Is he still alive?

00:23:47.236 --> 00:23:47.817
Nope.

00:23:50.642 --> 00:23:51.743
If you ask me,

00:23:52.124 --> 00:23:55.109
Mary spent her last living moments

00:23:55.572 --> 00:23:57.876
Trying to expose this guy's secret.

00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:01.222
But she never could.

00:24:03.385 --> 00:24:04.347
Where's she buried?

00:24:05.893 --> 00:24:06.695
She wasn't.

00:24:07.135 --> 00:24:07.937
She was cremated.

00:24:11.342 --> 00:24:14.027
What about that mirror?  It's not
in evidence lockup somewhere, is it?

00:24:15.847 --> 00:24:16.588
No.

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:20.415
It was returned to Mary's
family a long time ago.

00:24:22.037 --> 00:24:24.121
You have the names of
her family by any chance?

00:24:29.391 --> 00:24:31.356
I mean, you bring these
strangers into my house,

00:24:31.376 --> 00:24:32.919
And they ask me things like that?

00:24:32.959 --> 00:24:34.261
They were only trying to help.

00:24:34.361 --> 00:24:36.425
Please, Donna, you have to believe me.

00:24:36.625 --> 00:24:38.408
What? About bloody mary?

00:24:38.650 --> 00:24:40.774
Please, I know it sounds crazy.

00:24:41.134 --> 00:24:43.057
"Crazy" doesn't even begin to cover it.

00:24:43.278 --> 00:24:45.421
I mean, it's one thing for my
sister to believe this crap.

00:24:45.523 --> 00:24:47.367
She's 12. But you?

00:24:47.889 --> 00:24:48.851
Think about the way

00:24:49.632 --> 00:24:50.553
Your dad died,

00:24:50.994 --> 00:24:53.058
Okay, and the way Jill died.

00:24:54.382 --> 00:24:55.965
Okay, so...

00:24:57.107 --> 00:24:57.667
Bloody Mary.

00:24:57.708 --> 00:24:58.068
No!

00:24:58.108 --> 00:25:00.011
Bloody Mary. Bloody Mary.

00:25:02.978 --> 00:25:04.861
See? Nothing happened.

00:25:05.322 --> 00:25:06.604
Why would you do that?

00:25:07.145 --> 00:25:08.127
Oh, my god,

00:25:08.728 --> 00:25:10.751
There really is
something wrong with you.

00:25:22.627 --> 00:25:25.572
Elements that lose electrons become

00:25:25.712 --> 00:25:27.055
Positive ions,

00:25:27.596 --> 00:25:30.701
Which are smaller than other
atoms of the same element.

00:25:31.222 --> 00:25:33.766
Therefore, the ionic radius

00:25:33.897 --> 00:25:36.201
Is smaller than the atomic radius

00:25:41.435 --> 00:25:42.276
Charlie!

00:25:47.106 --> 00:25:47.868
Charlie!

00:25:52.818 --> 00:25:55.747
Charlie, stop it! What's
wrong? Just calm down!

00:25:58.855 --> 00:26:00.134
Charlie! Aah! Let me go!

00:26:00.264 --> 00:26:01.024
Charlie!

00:26:03.323 --> 00:26:04.065
Oh, really?

00:26:04.529 --> 00:26:06.642
Ah, that's too bad, Mr. Worthington.

00:26:07.208 --> 00:26:08.951
I would have paid a lot for that mirror.

00:26:08.988 --> 00:26:10.231
Okay, well, maybe next time.

00:26:10.453 --> 00:26:11.640
All right, thanks.

00:26:11.788 --> 00:26:12.493
So?

00:26:12.697 --> 00:26:14.551
So, that was Mary's brother.

00:26:14.727 --> 00:26:17.045
The mirror was in the family for years,

00:26:17.101 --> 00:26:18.436
Until he sold it

00:26:18.695 --> 00:26:19.789
One week ago

00:26:20.883 --> 00:26:22.867
To a store called estate antiques,

00:26:23.303 --> 00:26:24.861
A store in Toledo.

00:26:26.715 --> 00:26:28.755
So wherever the mirror
goes, that's where Mary goes?

00:26:29.005 --> 00:26:31.397
Her spirit's definitely
tied up with it somehow.

00:26:31.527 --> 00:26:34.512
Isn't there an old superstition that
says mirrors can capture spirits?

00:26:35.097 --> 00:26:37.285
Yeah, there is. When
someone would die in a house,

00:26:37.322 --> 00:26:39.825
People would cover up the mirrors
so the ghost wouldn't get trapped.

00:26:40.328 --> 00:26:42.561
This Mary dies in front of the
mirror, and it draws in her spirit.

00:26:42.850 --> 00:26:45.835
Yeah, but how could she move
through 100 different mirrors?

00:26:46.484 --> 00:26:48.014
I don't know but if the
mirror is the source,

00:26:48.033 --> 00:26:49.572
I say we find it and smash it.

00:26:50.925 --> 00:26:52.464
Yeah, I don't know. Maybe.

00:26:56.678 --> 00:26:57.327
Hello?

00:26:58.773 --> 00:26:59.496
Charlie?

00:27:18.557 --> 00:27:19.298
Hey.

00:27:20.244 --> 00:27:21.264
Hey. It's okay.

00:27:22.061 --> 00:27:23.767
You can open up your eyes, Charlie.

00:27:23.814 --> 00:27:25.575
It's okay, all right?

00:27:26.929 --> 00:27:27.745
Now, listen.

00:27:28.431 --> 00:27:29.729
You're gonna stay right here

00:27:30.331 --> 00:27:31.129
On this bed.

00:27:31.731 --> 00:27:33.178
You're not gonna look at glass

00:27:33.345 --> 00:27:35.347
Or anything else that
has a reflection, okay?

00:27:36.155 --> 00:27:37.341
As long as you do that

00:27:38.157 --> 00:27:39.585
She cannot get you.

00:27:42.691 --> 00:27:44.471
But I can't keep that up forever.

00:27:47.314 --> 00:27:48.798
I'm gonna die, aren't I?

00:27:50.707 --> 00:27:51.301
No.

00:27:52.895 --> 00:27:53.581
No.

00:27:55.371 --> 00:27:56.548
Not anytime soon.

00:27:58.746 --> 00:27:59.784
All right, Charlie,

00:28:00.470 --> 00:28:01.527
We need to know what happened.

00:28:02.510 --> 00:28:03.826
We were in the bathroom.

00:28:04.077 --> 00:28:04.967
Donna said it.

00:28:05.004 --> 00:28:06.561
That's not what we're talking about.

00:28:10.029 --> 00:28:11.586
Something happened, didn't it,

00:28:13.014 --> 00:28:14.015
In your life.

00:28:15.867 --> 00:28:16.645
A secret...

00:28:17.906 --> 00:28:19.140
Where someone got hurt?

00:28:25.110 --> 00:28:26.436
Can you tell us about it?

00:28:30.553 --> 00:28:31.721
I had this boyfriend.

00:28:34.680 --> 00:28:35.570
I loved him.

00:28:37.387 --> 00:28:39.681
But he kind of scared me, too, you know?

00:28:40.690 --> 00:28:41.560
And...

00:28:41.815 --> 00:28:42.729
One night

00:28:43.281 --> 00:28:44.428
At his house,

00:28:44.746 --> 00:28:45.893
We got in this fight.

00:28:48.293 --> 00:28:49.716
Then I broke up with him,

00:28:50.905 --> 00:28:53.093
And he got upset and he said

00:28:53.369 --> 00:28:55.726
He needed me and he loved me.

00:28:57.224 --> 00:28:58.179
And he said...

00:28:59.220 --> 00:29:02.130
"Charlie, if you walk out that door
right now, I'm gonna kill myself."

00:29:04.997 --> 00:29:06.441
And you know what I said?

00:29:08.061 --> 00:29:09.335
I said, "go ahead."

00:29:12.351 --> 00:29:13.562
And I left.

00:29:16.769 --> 00:29:18.107
How could I say that?

00:29:23.406 --> 00:29:25.254
How could I leave him like that?

00:29:28.340 --> 00:29:29.444
I just...

00:29:30.230 --> 00:29:32.142
I didn't believe him, you know?

00:29:39.043 --> 00:29:40.211
I should have.

00:29:49.336 --> 00:29:52.331
Her boyfriend killing himself,
that's not really Charlie's fault.

00:29:53.244 --> 00:29:54.369
You know as well as I do,

00:29:54.391 --> 00:29:57.131
Spirits don't exactly
see shades of gray,

00:29:57.194 --> 00:29:57.980
Dean.

00:29:58.373 --> 00:29:59.541
Charlie had a secret,

00:29:59.838 --> 00:30:00.815
Someone died.

00:30:01.367 --> 00:30:02.514
That's good enough for Mary.

00:30:03.321 --> 00:30:04.298
I guess.

00:30:04.957 --> 00:30:06.167
You know,I've been thinking,

00:30:07.112 --> 00:30:09.809
It might not be enough
to just smash that mirror.

00:30:10.404 --> 00:30:11.466
Why, what do you mean?

00:30:11.742 --> 00:30:13.059
Mary's hard to pin down, right?

00:30:13.123 --> 00:30:14.822
And she moves around
from mirror to mirror.

00:30:14.843 --> 00:30:17.829
So, who's to say that she's not gonna
just keep hiding in them forever?

00:30:19.252 --> 00:30:20.441
So maybe...

00:30:21.737 --> 00:30:23.245
We should try to pin her down,

00:30:24.356 --> 00:30:26.565
You know, summon her to her mirror

00:30:27.415 --> 00:30:28.604
And then smash it.

00:30:29.241 --> 00:30:30.622
Well, how do you know that's gonna work?

00:30:30.686 --> 00:30:31.471
I don't,

00:30:32.172 --> 00:30:33.383
I'm not for sure.

00:30:35.993 --> 00:30:37.352
Well, who's gonnasummon her?

00:30:39.157 --> 00:30:39.901
I will.

00:30:42.046 --> 00:30:43.299
She'll come after me.

00:30:45.242 --> 00:30:47.111
All right, you know what? That's it.

00:30:57.349 --> 00:30:58.730
This is about Jessica, isn't it?

00:31:02.935 --> 00:31:04.252
You think that's your
dirty little secret,

00:31:04.273 --> 00:31:06.100
That you killed her somehow?

00:31:09.345 --> 00:31:11.511
Sam, this has got to stop, man.

00:31:13.146 --> 00:31:13.953
I mean,

00:31:14.315 --> 00:31:15.674
The nightmares and-And

00:31:15.790 --> 00:31:17.808
Calling her name out in
the middle of the night,

00:31:18.615 --> 00:31:19.974
It's gonna kill you.

00:31:21.291 --> 00:31:22.353
Now, listen to me.

00:31:23.755 --> 00:31:25.241
It wasn't your fault.

00:31:26.715 --> 00:31:29.519
If you want to blame something,
then blame the thing that killed her.

00:31:29.986 --> 00:31:31.473
Or, hell, why don't
you take a swing at me?

00:31:31.515 --> 00:31:34.000
I'm the one that dragged you
away from her the first place.

00:31:34.213 --> 00:31:35.360
I don't blame you.

00:31:35.905 --> 00:31:37.200
You shouldn't blame yourself,

00:31:37.625 --> 00:31:39.260
Because there's
nothingyou could've done.

00:31:39.409 --> 00:31:41.108
I could've warned her. About what?!

00:31:41.899 --> 00:31:43.556
You didn't know what was gonna happen.

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:46.104
And, besides,

00:31:46.274 --> 00:31:48.366
All of this isn't a secret.
I mean, I know all about it.

00:31:48.377 --> 00:31:49.906
It's not gonna work with Mary anyway.

00:31:50.235 --> 00:31:51.234
No, you don't.

00:31:52.720 --> 00:31:53.294
I don't what?

00:31:53.379 --> 00:31:55.630
You don't know all about it.

00:31:56.352 --> 00:31:57.775
I haven't told you everything.

00:31:59.943 --> 00:32:01.005
What are you talking about?

00:32:01.833 --> 00:32:03.978
It wouldn't really be a
secret if I told you, would it?

00:32:11.207 --> 00:32:11.950
No.

00:32:13.373 --> 00:32:14.414
I don't like it.

00:32:14.435 --> 00:32:15.986
It's not gonna happen. Forget it.

00:32:16.708 --> 00:32:18.917
Dean, that girl back
there is going to die

00:32:19.972 --> 00:32:21.777
Unless we do something about it.

00:32:22.563 --> 00:32:23.349
And you know what?

00:32:23.731 --> 00:32:26.641
Who knows how many more people
are gonna die after that?

00:32:28.107 --> 00:32:29.190
Now, we're doing this.

00:32:32.025 --> 00:32:34.213
You've got to let me do this.

00:33:01.813 --> 00:33:04.043
Well, that's just great.

00:33:13.834 --> 00:33:15.427
All right, let's start looking.

00:33:54.250 --> 00:33:55.822
Maybe they've already sold it.

00:34:01.525 --> 00:34:02.672
I don't think so.

00:34:15.304 --> 00:34:16.303
That's it.

00:34:19.361 --> 00:34:20.572
You sure about this?

00:34:37.467 --> 00:34:38.444
Bloody Mary.

00:34:41.545 --> 00:34:42.607
Bloody Mary.

00:34:54.223 --> 00:34:55.052
Bloody Mary.

00:35:05.360 --> 00:35:07.251
I'll go check that out.
Stay here. Be careful.

00:35:09.618 --> 00:35:11.254
Smash anything that moves.

00:35:22.610 --> 00:35:23.502
Crap.

00:35:42.036 --> 00:35:42.991
Hold on

00:35:43.246 --> 00:35:45.816
Whoa, guys, false alarm.

00:35:46.326 --> 00:35:47.473
I tripped the system.

00:35:47.590 --> 00:35:48.482
Who are you?

00:35:49.161 --> 00:35:50.266
I'm the boss's kid.

00:35:52.007 --> 00:35:53.452
You're Mr. Yamashiro's kid?

00:36:09.116 --> 00:36:10.199
Come on.

00:36:11.324 --> 00:36:12.535
Come into this one.

00:36:36.270 --> 00:36:37.321
It's your fault.

00:36:38.766 --> 00:36:39.849
You killed her.

00:36:43.566 --> 00:36:44.861
You killed Jessica.

00:36:48.492 --> 00:36:50.297
Like I said, I was adopted.

00:36:51.072 --> 00:36:51.858
Yeah.

00:36:54.577 --> 00:36:55.596
You know, I just

00:36:56.287 --> 00:36:58.432
I really don't have
timefor this right now.

00:37:04.485 --> 00:37:05.823
You never told her the truth,

00:37:06.513 --> 00:37:07.724
Who you really were.

00:37:08.467 --> 00:37:10.166
But it's more than that,isn't it?

00:37:11.122 --> 00:37:12.715
Those nightmares you've been having

00:37:13.150 --> 00:37:14.658
Of jessica dying,

00:37:15.104 --> 00:37:16.060
Screaming,

00:37:16.952 --> 00:37:17.823
Burning

00:37:18.524 --> 00:37:20.796
You had them for days before she died.

00:37:21.784 --> 00:37:22.804
Didn't you?!

00:37:25.352 --> 00:37:27.264
You were so desperateto ignore them,

00:37:27.285 --> 00:37:29.006
To believethey were just dreams.

00:37:29.664 --> 00:37:31.140
How could you ignore them like that?

00:37:31.777 --> 00:37:34.283
How could you leave her alone to die?

00:37:37.129 --> 00:37:38.786
You dreamt it would happen!

00:37:45.478 --> 00:37:46.264
Dude.

00:37:46.837 --> 00:37:48.281
Sammy, sammy!

00:37:50.161 --> 00:37:51.053
It's sam.

00:37:52.845 --> 00:37:54.035
God, are you okay?

00:37:54.226 --> 00:37:55.118
Uh, yeah.

00:37:57.157 --> 00:37:58.049
Come on, come on.

00:39:01.127 --> 00:39:03.272
You killed them!

00:39:03.718 --> 00:39:05.418
All those people!

00:39:05.803 --> 00:39:07.991
You killed them!

00:39:36.510 --> 00:39:37.402
Hey, sam?

00:39:38.332 --> 00:39:39.118
Yeah?

00:39:40.530 --> 00:39:43.674
That's got to be like
what, 600 years of bad luck?

00:40:08.039 --> 00:40:09.377
So this is really over?

00:40:11.227 --> 00:40:12.268
Yeah, it's over.

00:40:14.498 --> 00:40:15.348
Thank you.

00:40:27.261 --> 00:40:28.110
Charlie?

00:40:32.144 --> 00:40:33.546
Your boyfriend's death,

00:40:34.799 --> 00:40:36.561
You really should try
to forgive yourself.

00:40:37.326 --> 00:40:38.367
No matter what you did,

00:40:38.834 --> 00:40:40.066
You probably couldn't have stopped it.

00:40:42.561 --> 00:40:44.091
Sometimes bad things just happen.

00:40:55.775 --> 00:40:56.742
That's good advice.

00:41:13.272 --> 00:41:14.101
Hey, sam?

00:41:15.163 --> 00:41:15.800
Yeah?

00:41:16.788 --> 00:41:18.359
Now that this is all over,

00:41:19.336 --> 00:41:21.078
I want you to tell me
what that secret is.

00:41:26.016 --> 00:41:26.950
Look...

00:41:28.469 --> 00:41:29.467
You're my brother.

00:41:30.848 --> 00:41:32.165
And I'd die for you.

00:41:34.830 --> 00:41:36.869
But there are some things
I need to keep to myself.



00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
